a more nuanced understanding of business and organizational mechanics. Your grasp of the essentials will prepare you think practically about developing a competitive, profit-driven business strategy.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "Offered online only.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: students enrolled in the Executive Master of Human Resource Management program.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GR", "acadGroup": "IL", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2818, "crseId": 367552, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILRHR", "catalogNbr": "8105", "titleShort": "Align HR Strat with Org Strat", "titleLong": "Aligning HR Strategy with Organizational Strategy", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 2000, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "07/11/2022", "endDt": "07/24/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 3, "netid": "cjc53", "firstName": "Chris", "middleName": "J.", "lastName": "Collins"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Open only to students of the Executive Master of Human Resource Management program."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "07/11/2022", "endDt": "07/24/2022", "addConsent": "D", "addConsentDescr": "Department Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "OL", "instrModeDescrshort": "OL", "instrModeDescr": "Online", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 0.5, "unitsMaximum": 0.5, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2022", "sessionEndDt": "08/20/2022", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "A thorough understanding of your organization's value creation model and ability to develop competencies through processes, technology, and people are essential to ensuring that the HR organization is aligned vertically and horizontally to produce superior results. With this understanding, HR will be able to articulate how it can improve processes, people and customer outcomes, and financial results. This course develops the skills needed to assess how organizations create value and to align the HR function to execute the organization's strategy. Participants analyze the Balanced Scorecard approach as a means of vertically aligning the HR system with organizational objectives. They learn how to create a vertical-alignment strategy and use it to improve HR decision-making, people outcomes, processes, customer outcomes, and financial results. And they learn the skills required to plan and assess horizontal alignment of HR systems and practices. Finally, the course discusses best practices related to workforce partitioning, performance variability, value identification, and employee impact.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "Offered online only.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: students enrolled in the Executive Master of Human Resource Management.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GR", "acadGroup": "IL", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2818, "crseId": 368342, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILRHR", "catalogNbr": "8106", "titleShort": "Understanding Fin Statements", "titleLong": "Understanding Financial Statements", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1999, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "06/20/2022", "endDt": "07/06/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 3, "netid": "cjc53", "firstName": "Chris", "middleName": "J.", "lastName": "Collins"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "06/20/2022", "endDt": "07/06/2022", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "OL", "instrModeDescrshort": "OL", "instrModeDescr": "Online", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 0.5, "unitsMaximum": 0.5, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2022", "sessionEndDt": "08/20/2022", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "Every company's finance department keeps detailed records of the daily transactions involved in the running the organization. Periodically, they create reports that allow management, stakeholders and regulating authorities to have insight into the financial health of the firm. This course will develops the skills needed to understand both the metrics that are reported in income statements, balance sheets, and cash flow statements, and how they relate to each other. You will also learn how comparing numbers across your company and the industry from year to year can help you assess the overall financial performance of the firm.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "Offered online only.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: students enrolled in the Executive Master of Human Resource Management.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GR", "acadGroup": "IL", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2818, "crseId": 367567, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILRHR", "catalogNbr": "8107", "titleShort": "Strategic Talent Analytics", "titleLong": "Strategic Talent Analytics", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 2001, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "07/25/2022", "endDt": "08/07/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 3, "netid": "cjc53", "firstName": "Chris", "middleName": "J.", "lastName": "Collins"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Open only to students of the Executive Master of Human Resource Management program."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "07/25/2022", "endDt": "08/07/2022", "addConsent": "D", "addConsentDescr": "Department Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "OL", "instrModeDescrshort": "OL", "instrModeDescr": "Online", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 0.5, "unitsMaximum": 0.5, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2022", "sessionEndDt": "08/20/2022", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "HR leaders help drive business performance by delivering competitive advantage through people. Performance relies on measures, so you need to be adept at planning and interpreting your organization's \"people metrics.\" This requires a solid grasp of HR analytics: the systematic collection, analysis, and interpretation of data designed to improve decisions about talent and the organization as a whole. The use of analytics is changing the way HR professionals quantify the value that people\u2014our biggest asset\u2014have on the organization's ability to succeed in the market or in its mission. In this course, you take a strategic view of your organization's use of HR data and its measurement systems. The course prepares you to determine the HR metrics that align with your company's strategic goals. It explains the characteristics of high quality data and equips you to find and collect that data, inside or outside your organization. It provides a high-level introduction to common analysis techniques and some mistakes to avoid when interpreting data, or when assessing reports and interpretations offered by others. In the final section of the course, you will learn to take the results of your data collection and analysis and communicate your findings in a compelling manner so that change follows.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: students enrolled in the Executive Master of Human Resource Management.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GR", "acadGroup": "IL", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2818, "crseId": 371077, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILRHR", "catalogNbr": "8702", "titleShort": "Using Design Thinking", "titleLong": "Using Design Thinking in Human Resources", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1634, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "05/30/2022", "endDt": "06/12/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "cjc53", "firstName": "Chris", "middleName": "J.", "lastName": "Collins"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "05/30/2022", "endDt": "06/12/2022", "addConsent": "D", "addConsentDescr": "Department Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "OL", "instrModeDescrshort": "OL", "instrModeDescr": "Online", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "C", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 1, "unitsMaximum": 1, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBas